  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_60641689",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: latinos_will_do_anything_to_get_into_trump_s_america; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts people climbing a border fence with the overlaid text 'latinos will do anything to get into trump's america.' This meme uses a visual of border crossing, which is mapped onto the text to imply that Latinos are desperate or willing to risk everything to enter the United States under a Trump administration. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that falls under 'Anti-Latino/Hispanic Stereotypes' in the provided knowledge base, specifically targeting immigration status assumptions and portraying Latinos as inherently criminal or desperate. The intent is to dehumanize and stigmatize a specific ethnic group based on their immigration status, which is a direct attack on protected characteristics and promotes xenophobic and racist attitudes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_42c48086"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a373ad18",
